# Meta Rules

E2E UI automation for **ThriveSparrow** using Playwright + JavaScript ES modules, Page Object Model via POManager.

## Rule Inventory

This project distributes rules into the folders they govern. Understand their scope before generating code:

| Rule File | Type | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| `.cursor/rules/meta.mdc` | Always | Rule interpretation, precedence, coding standards (this file) |
| `.cursor/rules/project-context.mdc` | Always | Product domain, application modules, framework architecture, commands |
| `TSAP/Pages/README.md` | Folder-local | POM pattern, POManager, page object template, method patterns |
| `TSAP/Pages/locator-rules.md` | Folder-local | Locator priority P1–P6.1, naming prefixes, XPath, anti-patterns |
| `TSAP/Pages/function-rules.md` | Folder-local | Function naming, options objects, JSDoc, anti-patterns |
| `TSAP/Pages/pwactions-reference.md` | Folder-local | PwActions API reference — click, input, wait, query, navigation methods |
| `TSAP/Tests/README.md` | Folder-local | Test folder overview, test generation workflow (Phases 0–5), Jira/Figma integration |
| `TSAP/Tests/test-rules.md` | Folder-local | thrivePage fixture, test structure, assertions, Allure, test data isolation |
| `TSAP/Tests/WebApp_Testing/{Module}_Test_Cases/README.md` | Module-local | Product context, page objects, common patterns per module |
| `TSAP/Data/README.md` | Folder-local | Environment config, constants, EntityIds, YAML data |
| `TSAP/Fixtures/README.md` | Folder-local | thrivePage fixture internals, network monitoring, failure artifacts |
| `TSAP/Shared_Functions/README.md` | Folder-local | Cross-page utilities, when to add shared vs page-specific |

## Rule Precedence

When rules overlap or conflict, apply this order (highest priority first):

1. **Module documentation** (`{Module}_Test_Cases/README.md`) — module-specific patterns always override generic rules.
2. **Domain-specific rules** (`locator-rules.md`, `function-rules.md`, `test-rules.md`) — the authority for their domain.
3. **Folder README** (`Pages/README.md`, `Tests/README.md`, etc.) — structural context and conventions.
4. **This meta rule** — universal coding standards and routing; lowest specificity.

