## MCP Tool Routing

| Trigger | MCP Server | Primary Tools |
|---|---|---|
| Jira ticket ID mentioned | `user-mcp-atlassian` | `jira_get_issue`, `confluence_get_page` — fetch ticket + PRD + Figma link |
| Figma URL present | `user-twigs-ai-mcp` | `get_figma_screenshot`, `get_figma_json` — extract UI structure for locators |
| Debugging / exploring app | `user-playwright-browser` | `browser_navigate`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_click` — always snapshot first |

**Jira:** Always fetch PRD (Confluence) and Figma if linked in ticket — Jira alone is never enough.
**Figma:** Start with screenshot, fall back to JSON. If 404 (expired token), proceed without it.
**Browser:** Always `browser_snapshot()` before any interaction. Never copy raw `[ref=…]` into page objects.

### Browser Environment: Always Use S2

Always navigate to `https://test-automation-2.s2.engagesparrow.com/login` (admin: `thrive.automation+10@surveysparrowqa.com` / `Test@1234`) for locator discovery. Never use any other environment.

### Hard Gate: Browser Verification for New Locators

**NEVER write new locators without first navigating to the live app and running `browser_snapshot()`.** This applies to ALL new page objects and ALL new locators added to existing page objects.

- If writing a new page object → navigate to the feature URL, snapshot every screen in the flow, extract locators from the real DOM.
- If the app is unreachable (no credentials, environment down) → STOP and ask the user. Do NOT invent placeholder locators.
- Pipe-separated fallback locators (`locator1 | locator2`) are a rule violation — they indicate the locator was guessed, not verified.
- This rule has **no exceptions**. Skipping browser verification is as serious as using raw `page.click()` instead of `PwActions`.

