## Rule Quality Guidelines

When creating or updating rules or READMEs in this project:
- Keep every file under 200 lines. Split large rules into separate files.
- One domain per file. Never mix locator rules with test structure rules.
- Be assertive. Use "Always", "Must", "Never" — not "Consider" or "Try to".
- Include concrete examples — at least one good and one bad per rule.
- Rules live in the folder they govern. Only project-wide rules (`meta.mdc`, `project-context.mdc`) live in `.cursor/rules/`.
